    {
      "id": "3a06e46f50ae673b4546d4ae0126d19d84e7e512",
      "short_id": "3a06e46f",
      "created_at": "2025-08-17T22:10:04.000-07:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "f3f990bd86d041a01e7012cc55bf9bb03a0fd445"
      ],
      "title": "Add HTTP/3 quic stream id field.",
      "message": "Add HTTP/3 quic stream id field.\n\nIt is currently impossible to do proper connection tracking outside of wireshark. The problem is subtle:\n - A single UDP packet can have data from multiple QUIC stream ids\n - A single QUIC stream can have multiple HTTP/3 frames in it\n - With the current layout, it is impossible to tell which quic stream belongs to which http3 frame in a single packet.\n\nThis adds http3.frame_streamid that contains the QUIC stream id for each HTTP/3 frame.\n",
      "author_name": "Mike Kaplinskiy",
      "author_email": "mike@ladderlife.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-08-14T09:47:43.000-07:00",
      "committer_name": "Mike Kaplinskiy",
      "committer_email": "mike@ladderlife.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-08-17T22:10:04.000-07:00",
